Title: Distributed Web Infrastructure (3 servers with HAProxy)
Goal: www.foobar.com behind a load balancer, 2 web/app servers, 1 DB.

ASCII diagram:
[User] -> [DNS] -> [HAProxy LB] -> [Web+App #1] -> [MySQL]
                                  \-> [Web+App #2] -> [MySQL]

Added & why:
- Load Balancer (HAProxy): spreads requests, improves availability/throughput
- Two Web+App servers: remove app-tier SPOF, enable horizontal scaling
- Dedicated DB server: separate concerns, tuning/backups

LB algorithm (example: Round Robin): cycles through backends in order
Active-Active vs Active-Passive: AA = both serve; AP = one serves, one standby

DB Primary-Replica:
- Primary handles writes; replicas receive async replication; reads can go to replicas
App view: Primary = read/write; Replica = read-only

Issues remaining:
- SPOF: single DB primary; single LB
- Security: no firewalls, no HTTPS
- Observability: no monitoring/logging
